{"inputs": {"input": {"question": "How do work and non-work usag differ in ChatGPT, and how does this relate to usage for work and non-work purposess?"}, "config": null}, "outputs": {"output": "Work and non-work usage of ChatGPT differ in their growth rates and focus areas. According to the context, non-work queries have been increasing faster than work-related queries. For work purposes, ChatGPT usage is primarily focused on obtaining, documenting, and interpreting information, as well as making decisions, giving advice, solving problems, and thinking creatively. Writing is the most common work-related use, accounting for about 40-42% of work messages, with many requests involving editing or modifying existing text. In contrast, non-work usage is growing more rapidly overall, suggesting that welfare gains from generative AI usage outside work could be substantial. Thus, while work usage is centered around productivity and decision support in knowledge-intensive jobs, non-work usage is expanding faster, indicating broader lifestyle or personal benefits."}, "session_id": "5537da3f-7c64-411e-a641-538327a63654", "error": null, "extra": {"metadata": {"revision_id": "default_chain_init", "num_repetitions": 1, "example_version": "2025-10-04T19:30:42.913181+00:00", "ls_method": "traceable", "ls_example_context": ["<1-hop>

