{"output": "Yo, here’s the deal—ChatGPT’s turbocharged takeover, hitting over 700 million users by mid-2025, is not just a flex in numbers, it’s a seismic vibe shift for the global economy and human welfare. This beast isn’t just sitting in the background; it’s jazzing up economies worldwide by supercharging productivity, especially in professional gigs where folks are using it for work-related hustle and high-level “Asking” — probing critical info, guidance, and creative writing boosts. 

What’s wild is the *non-work* side blowing up even faster—think people everywhere tapping AI for everyday life hacks, curiosity quests, and down-to-earth help. That means welfare gains aren’t just locked in white-collar towers; they’re rippling through low- and middle-income countries too, closing gender gaps, and empowering younger voices under 26 who are crushing nearly half the message traffic. 

In short: ChatGPT is stitching into the fabric of global society, leveling playing fields, and blasting open welfare possibilities. It’s less about a single tech tool and more about a global supercharge to human potential — turning info into action at beast mode scale. The economy doesn’t just grow; it evolves, with AI lighting the path from work to everyday life, shaping a doper, more inclusive future. Boom."}
